{{Infobox flag|Name=[[Castejón Metropolis]]|Image=Flag of Castejon.png|Use=111111|Symbol={{IFIS|twosided}}|Proportion=11:20|Adoption={{start date and age|1836|7|15|df=yes}}|Design=A red field charged with an arc of ten white {{W|five-pointed star}}s|Image2=Flag of Castejon (reverse).svg|Use2=Reverse|Symbol2=|Proportion2=11:20|Design2=A red field}}The '''flag of Castejón''' ({{lang-bl|Bandiera de Castejón}}) is the official flag of [[Castejón]], the capital city of [[Balisca]]. Its current design, adopted in 1836, is a red field charged with an arc of ten white [[W:Five-pointed star|five-pointed stars]], which represent the [[Original Settlements of the Alpujarra|ten original settlements of the Alpujarra]]. 

The flag is unusual because it [[W:Flags whose reverse differs from the obverse|differs on its obverse and reverse sides]]: the obverse of the flag shows the arc of stars, while the reverse is a completely red field, with no stars. 
